{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-945193085b843eb0", "type": "tool_result", "content": "Paper 2607.26742 not found\n===\n# Mega-TTS: Zero-Shot Text-to-Speech at Scale with Intrinsic Inductive Bias\narXiv: 2306.03509\nAuthors: Ziyue Jiang, Yi Ren, Zhenhui Ye, Jinglin Liu, Chen Zhang, Qian Yang, Shengpeng Ji, Rongjie Huang, Chunfeng Wang, Xiang Yin, Zejun Ma, Zhou Zhao\nYear: 2023 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose Mega-TTS, a zero-shot text-to-speech system that decomposes mel-spectrograms into content, timbre, prosody, and phase attributes and models each according to its intrinsic properties.\n  2. We train Mega-TTS on a multi-domain and multi-lingual dataset containing 20K hours of speech data, scaling beyond traditional single-domain audiobook corpora.\n  3. We evaluate Mega-TTS on zero-shot TTS, speech editing, and cross-lingual TTS tasks, and propose a novel sampling strategy for speech editing using discrete prosody tokens.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多说话人, TTS/功能-语音编辑", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "88a051b7-0d55-432d-af3b-981d020158bb", "uuid": "3270b60a-918e-478d-a473-4028d65ea9f2", "timestamp": "2026-07-30T08:20:57.980Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "Paper 2607.26742 not found\n===\n# Mega-TTS: Zero-Shot Text-to-Speech at Scale with Intrinsic Inductive Bias\narXiv: 2306.03509\nAuthors: Ziyue Jiang, Yi Ren, Zhenhui Ye, Jinglin Liu, Chen Zhang, Qian Yang, Shengpeng Ji, Rongjie Huang, Chunfeng Wang, Xiang Yin, Zejun Ma, Zhou Zhao\nYear: 2023 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose Mega-TTS, a zero-shot text-to-speech system that decomposes mel-spectrograms into content, timbre, prosody, and phase attributes and models each according to its intrinsic properties.\n  2. We train Mega-TTS on a multi-domain and multi-lingual dataset containing 20K hours of speech data, scaling beyond traditional single-domain audiobook corpora.\n  3. We evaluate Mega-TTS on zero-shot TTS, speech editing, and cross-lingual TTS tasks, and propose a novel sampling strategy for speech editing using discrete prosody tokens.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多说话人, TTS/功能-语音编辑", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
